{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>hasty for wealth</b> — like the interpretation 'hastens to grow rich,' meaning: one who is hasty and rushes to gather wealth is called an evil man, [with] an evil eye, as in: 'and your eye be evil.'" "<b>lacks</b> — when he gathers it and does not give from it to the poor."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Resolved the abbreviation 'כפירוש' as introducing a comparison to the standard interpretation of an adjacent phrase; the final scriptural allusion is to Deuteronomy 15:9."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:17.534019350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}